<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">occĭdŭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		2. occĭdo, I.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Going down</i>, <i>setting</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-class. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sole jam fere occiduo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					19, 7, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">occiduo sole,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 63</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oriens occiduusque dies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					4, 832</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Calp.
					Ecl. 3, 82</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 3, 33</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoebus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 14, 416</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>western</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab occiduo sole,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					5, 558</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">occiduae aquae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 1, 314</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">occiduae primaeque domus,</span>”
				<i>in the west and in the east</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 1, 4, 73</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Th. 1, 200</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mauri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					3, 294</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 2, 621</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hora,</span>”
				<i>the evening hour</i>, <i>hour of sunset</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Calp.
					Ecl. 5, 34</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">occiduus (sc. sol),</span>”
				<i>the west</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. 5, 35, 8</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Sinking</i>, <i>failing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">labitur occiduae per iter declive senectae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 15, 227</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Frail</i>, <i>perishable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exsortes animae carnis ab occiduo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Paul. Nol. Carm. 34, 306</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
